  "note": "Synthetic ids only. host_state.messages maps a conversation id to its stored rows, oldest first, served by a copy of the App Server's paging (letta.js 0.34.39 listConversationMessagePage over its strict local store). A row {\"synthetic_image_return\": n, ...} stands for an image tool return whose base64 data is n bytes of 'A' (the file would otherwise be over 2 MB); expected responses use the same marker. Each row is served through the wrapper's turn identity ledger, which backfills it: the user row opens turn otid-1, every other row is <id>:<message_type>.",
